  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Lut, his family, the angels and the people of the city are never drawn; no plate starts on an imperative to Lut. A moon from «الليل» (it lives across the reciter's repeats of 65:7-8 and 65:14), an hourglass for the decree (66), gone before the city's people come (67). 65:8-11 «ولا يلتفت منكم أحد» is not glossed (Al-Muyassar: beware of turning; As-Sa'di: hurry). 66:1-4 is not glossed (both tafsirs paraphrase in Allah's first person). STAGING v4: Restaged under Staging v4: Lut is a blue drop labelled Lut, the messengers one gold drop labelled 'the angels' (no number: neither tafsir gives one), in his town. 61-64: the angels arrive (61:2), Lut speaks, the angels answer; a seal on 64:2. 65: at night his family (an uncountable faceless believers group; Al-Muyassar: his believing family) walks ahead and Lut follows behind them; nobody turns round; his wife is never drawn. 66: a glow on Lut on 66:2 (Allah informed him), hourglass for the decree; no punishment event in this video. 67: the people of the city (uncountable, faceless) come and speak to one another (rejoicing at the news); their intent is never shown."
 },
